      <reaction id="mw6da69e10_4820_40a8_96cc_6d8e32ae4d16" name="Reaction_52" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Tumor-local CD8 proliferation, SATURATING in density (Blessin-anchored k_pro; rho_CD8_max*V_T is the half-saturation density, NOT a hard ceiling). Reformulated 2026-07-13 from the logistic k_pro*CD8*(1 - CD8/cap): see notes/model/tcell_carrying_capacity_inversion.md. The logistic has no max(0,.) clamp, so once GVAX drove CD8 past the cap the &quot;proliferation&quot; reaction ran as a QUADRATIC SINK whose strength scaled with k_pro -- raising CD8 proliferation destroyed CD8 (4x k_CD8_T_pro -&gt; 0.775x CD8), and influx sensitivity was crushed to a square root. The pools sit AT the cap boundary (d21 CD8/cap ~1.1 at the submodel-anchored theta), so the sign flipped exactly where the model lives. The saturating form is monotone in k_pro and in influx at every density, so behaviour no longer depends on which side of the cap a draw lands. The pool is bounded by k_CD8_death (restored 2026-06-22), not by the cap. Influx/turnover sets the level -- as this comment always claimed, but which the logistic did not deliver.</body>
        </notes>
        <listOfProducts>
          <speciesReference species="mw4d86ebfe_974f_4a04_9638_e0e464e3b17c" stoichiometry="1"/>
        </listOfProducts>
        <kineticLaw>
          <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
            <apply>
              <divide/>
              <apply>
                <times/>
                <ci> mw286d0f62_d972_48d5_ae24_de7ee053388a </ci>
                <ci> mw4d86ebfe_974f_4a04_9638_e0e464e3b17c </ci>
              </apply>
              <apply>
                <plus/>
                <cn type="integer"> 1 </cn>
                <apply>
                  <divide/>
                  <ci> mw4d86ebfe_974f_4a04_9638_e0e464e3b17c </ci>
                  <apply>
                    <plus/>
                    <apply>
                      <times/>
                      <ci> mw0b05a207_bca8_4926_9f3e_8ed74f9cf820 </ci>
                      <ci> mw4906f192_367e_4550_8473_143fd7b685b1 </ci>
                    </apply>
                    <ci> mw7111dd2d_c72a_48bd_974b_3de5fe5d69c6 </ci>
                  </apply>
                </apply>
              </apply>
            </apply>
          </math>
        </kineticLaw>
      </reaction>
      <reaction id="mw4bd61ade_57f8_47c4_8927_c5c333910987" name="Reaction_53" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Tumor-local homeostatic CD8 death with a density-dependent CROWDING term (V3 stabilizer, 2026-07-17). Linear apoptosis/AICD k_CD8_death*CD8 plus a quadratic crowding death k_CD8_death*CD8^2/(rho_CD8_crowd*V_T) representing cytokine/nutrient competition (per-cell survival drops as local CD8 density rises). The crowding term is NOT meant to lower the target CD8 level -- it removes the near-critical runaway. With linear birth vs linear death the in-tumor CD8 balance sits at a bifurcation (below it CD8 collapses, above it the coupled tumour/immune loop diverges to NaN; ~30% of prior draws blow up and the ~62 cells/mm^2 target lives on that edge). The C^2 death bounds the high-density branch, converting the explode side into a finite steady state so the high-density regime becomes reachable. Crowding equals the linear death at density = rho_CD8_crowd (2e7 cell/mL ~ 220 cells/mm^2), ~28% extra death at the target. Distinct from exhaustion routing.</body>
        </notes>
        <listOfReactants>
          <speciesReference species="mw4d86ebfe_974f_4a04_9638_e0e464e3b17c" stoichiometry="1"/>
        </listOfReactants>
        <kineticLaw>
          <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
            <apply>
              <times/>
              <ci> mwc78b36fa_67c0_4452_b0ea_a8a2dad5c716 </ci>
              <ci> mw4d86ebfe_974f_4a04_9638_e0e464e3b17c </ci>
              <apply>
                <plus/>
                <cn type="integer"> 1 </cn>
                <apply>
                  <divide/>
                  <ci> mw4d86ebfe_974f_4a04_9638_e0e464e3b17c </ci>
                  <apply>
                    <plus/>
                    <apply>
                      <times/>
                      <ci> mw2a3e5298_3f39_4049_8c4e_cb5f22c75812 </ci>
                      <ci> mw4906f192_367e_4550_8473_143fd7b685b1 </ci>
                    </apply>
                    <ci> mw7111dd2d_c72a_48bd_974b_3de5fe5d69c6 </ci>
                  </apply>
                </apply>
              </apply>
            </apply>
          </math>
        </kineticLaw>
      </reaction>
