      <reaction id="mwed92d4fb_e2d3_4545_828b_489c54ea2f9e" name="Reaction_182" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Tumor-local Th renewal, SATURATING in density (rho_Th_max*V_T is the half-saturation density, NOT a hard ceiling). Reformulated 2026-07-13 from the logistic k_pro*Th*(1 - Th/cap) -- same defect as CD8, see notes/model/tcell_carrying_capacity_inversion.md: unclamped, so above the cap the reaction became a quadratic sink scaling with k_Th_pro_tumor, inverting the response. Th sits at ~1.1x the cap at d21 under GVAX (submodel-anchored theta), i.e. right on the sign flip. The saturating form is monotone in k_pro and influx at every density. Bounded by k_CD4_death (restored 2026-06-22), not by the cap. The CD8-inflammation Hill (alpha_Th_cap, route-2) was retired 2026-06-22. k_Th_pro_tumor keeps its Ki67 anchor. Mechanism-specific losses: Th-&gt;Treg conversion, Th-&gt;Th_exh exhaustion, Th_exh death via k_cell_clear.</body>
        </notes>
        <listOfProducts>
          <speciesReference species="mw6bd25160_21b9_4762_842b_afd518b4a48f" stoichiometry="1"/>
        </listOfProducts>
        <kineticLaw>
          <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
            <apply>
              <divide/>
              <apply>
                <times/>
                <ci> mwf0a9c502_184a_4e1a_adef_ef1f0b7098d7 </ci>
                <ci> mw6bd25160_21b9_4762_842b_afd518b4a48f </ci>
              </apply>
              <apply>
                <plus/>
                <cn type="integer"> 1 </cn>
                <apply>
                  <divide/>
                  <ci> mw6bd25160_21b9_4762_842b_afd518b4a48f </ci>
                  <apply>
                    <plus/>
                    <apply>
                      <times/>
                      <ci> mw72b3bfd4_558f_43d9_b7df_fb3bb43b5f07 </ci>
                      <ci> mw4906f192_367e_4550_8473_143fd7b685b1 </ci>
                    </apply>
                    <ci> mw7111dd2d_c72a_48bd_974b_3de5fe5d69c6 </ci>
                  </apply>
                </apply>
              </apply>
            </apply>
          </math>
        </kineticLaw>
      </reaction>
      <reaction id="mwd8505d46_6dd3_47fb_bcfa_130e18944efc" name="Reaction_183" reversible="false">
