          <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Antigen transfer from GVAX-derived mcDC2 to LN-resident cDC1 (Ferris 2022). Catalytic by design: mcDC2 is the antigen donor and is not consumed (one migratory DC cross-dresses many resident cDC1). No antigen species moves in this reaction, so there is nothing to conserve here -- it is a count-gated cDC1-&gt;mcDC1 maturation; the antigen-LOAD dependence enters downstream at the H_P1-gated CD8 priming step (Teff_module). Bounded, not runaway: V_LN.cDC1 is the consumed substrate and is replenished only by its homeostatic source (APC_module), and the effective first-order rate k_cDC1_Ag_transfer*mcDC2 ~ 1e-3..1e-1/day stays well below cDC1 turnover. Audit m1-A11: no change.</body>
        </notes>
        <listOfReactants>
          <speciesReference species="mw7bf7eca1_2c45_4048_9396_1a283564e7a7" stoichiometry="1"/>
        </listOfReactants>
        <listOfProducts>
          <speciesReference species="mw657002ab_7e04_4c24_85b8_56e410eeed49" stoichiometry="1"/>
        </listOfProducts>
        <kineticLaw>
          <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
            <apply>
              <times/>
              <ci> mw5a37b69d_3d1c_426a_9a56_121212d26de1 </ci>
              <ci> mw7bf7eca1_2c45_4048_9396_1a283564e7a7 </ci>
              <ci> mweb08ab29_b4dc_41f5_a68c_6515d4a8585a </ci>
            </apply>
          </math>
        </kineticLaw>
      </reaction>
